        {
          "text": "NING Wan-wo 寧完我, d. 1665, Chinese bannerman of the Plain Red Banner, was a native of Liao-tung. Having pledged his allegiance to the Manchus under Nurhaci [q. v.], he served with Sahaliyen [q. v.], third son of Daišan [q. v.], until 1629.",
          "source": "eccp-3649160",
          "kind": "source-wording",
          "status": "imported"
        },
        {
          "text": "寧完我，字公甫，遼陽人。",
          "source": "qsg-volume-232",
          "kind": "biographical-opening",
          "status": "proposed"
        }
      ]
    },
